Added a helper method to **src/main.js**:

```js
export class MuJuCoDemo {
  setMotorSpeed(motorName, speed){
    // Find actuator index by name
    const idx = this.model.actuator_names.findIndex(n=>n===motorName);
    if(idx>=0){
      this.data.ctrl[idx]=speed;
    } else {
      console.warn('Motor', motorName,'not found');
    }
  }
```

You can now control a motor (e.g., the left motor of the hexacopter) from JavaScript with:

```js
demo.setMotorSpeed('left_motor', 5.0);
```

